And, you know, I think you put it really well, April.

522
00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:36.030
There's a side of Angela you don't know unless you play tennis with her.

523
00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.330
Well, yeah, that's right.

524
00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:44.150
So she'll show up to play tennis in the Angela that we all know and love, right?

525
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:51.470
Where she, like, arrives and she has, like, a granola from Josh and some little gift for us and some sweet story.

526
00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:52.610
And she's, like...

527
00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.990
She's sure it's made for everybody.

528
00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:59.750
She's sure she brought me a hummingbird feeder and, like, you know, like, all these beautiful things.

529
00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:01.410
Here's the new tea I have.

530
00:24:01.510 --> 00:24:02.570
You have to try it.

531
00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:05.170
The most considerate person ever.

532
00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:05.830
Oh, considerate.

533
00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:06.090
Yes.

534
00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.230
Literally, like, the kindest, sweetest, most considerate.

535
00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:10.830
And then we get on the court, right?

536
00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:12.210
Yeah.

537
00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:12.870
She's like the Hulk.

538
00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:16.610
She is.

539
00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:18.650
There's a Jekyll and Hyde.

540
00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:19.710
Yes.

541
00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:23.150
But not, like, she's not mean.

542
00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:28.530
She's just really competitive and in cutthroat.

543
00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:33.890
So she has this shot and we call it the Angela because it's a really good shot.

544
00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:40.390
She's got a very good forehand and she has this shot where she does a really deep angle.

545
00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:43.410
And it's very, very difficult to get to.

546
00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:48.570
And, you know, okay, that's fine.

547
00:24:49.030 --> 00:24:53.410
And the first, like, three times she does it and scores points.

548
00:24:53.410 --> 00:24:59.350
By the way, when she's up, like, like in the game we play, you know, the winner wins 11.

549
00:24:59.630 --> 00:25:03.430
Like, when her team is up, like, 7-2, she's still doing that.

550
00:25:03.430 --> 00:25:05.150
And that's when I get really mad.

551
00:25:07.570 --> 00:25:09.810
I get mad at, like, three or four, I'll say.

552
00:25:10.390 --> 00:25:10.610
Yeah.

553
00:25:12.090 --> 00:25:13.230
I'm a little earlier.

554
00:25:13.410 --> 00:25:15.190
And I'm actually mad.

555
00:25:15.330 --> 00:25:16.650
And I'll go, keep it up.

556
00:25:17.050 --> 00:25:17.990
Keep it up, Angela.

557
00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:19.650
Let's see where that gets you.

558
00:25:19.890 --> 00:25:21.350
And I'm so clearly mad.

559
00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:25.150
And she's like, he has no idea that I'm really mad.

560
00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:27.890
It's like, I'm going to kill you.

561
00:25:29.630 --> 00:25:34.450
Or the other thing she did to you, Rebecca, the little, like, sometimes she's like a little tip of the hat.

562
00:25:34.450 --> 00:25:35.250
And you're like, yeah.

563
00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:36.430
Oh, don't do that.

564
00:25:36.930 --> 00:25:41.250
It's like she'll do a really wicked shot and then almost curtsy to you.

565
00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:44.310
She does.

566
00:25:44.430 --> 00:25:45.550
She has a little leg kick.

567
00:25:45.710 --> 00:25:47.090
She has a little, like, a leg kick.

568
00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:47.550
Yeah.

569
00:25:47.550 --> 00:25:49.630
When you're like, aren't you adorable?

570
00:25:51.410 --> 00:25:56.430
We had a fill-in for this woman who is only in town periodically.

571
00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:57.690
And she's Danish.

572
00:25:58.050 --> 00:26:02.210
And she is hilarious because she curses in Danish.

573
00:26:04.470 --> 00:26:06.630
And Angela hit two shots back-to-back.

574
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:07.690
One was in Angla.

575
00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:12.370
And then one was this really mean backhand drop shot.

576
00:26:12.670 --> 00:26:14.070
Charlotte cursed at her in Danish.

577
00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:15.990
And I have no idea what she said.

578
00:26:16.170 --> 00:26:17.890
And I was on the same side as Charlotte.

579
00:26:18.370 --> 00:26:20.950
And I said, oh, my gosh, I'd love to know what you said.

580
00:26:21.090 --> 00:26:22.490
And she was like, you really don't want to know.

581
00:26:22.770 --> 00:26:23.730
And I was like, it's okay.

582
00:26:24.530 --> 00:26:25.450
I was like, it's okay.

583
00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:27.650
We cursed at her in English all the time.

584
00:26:27.710 --> 00:26:31.270
You can actually tell her what you said.

585
00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:33.490
Angela.

586
00:26:36.430 --> 00:26:37.930
Can you see it, Sam?

587
00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:40.410
I can absolutely see the curtsying thing.

588
00:26:40.610 --> 00:26:42.390
I know exactly the leg kick.

589
00:26:42.550 --> 00:26:43.490
I know the leg kick.

590
00:26:43.790 --> 00:26:44.130
Yep.

591
00:26:44.410 --> 00:26:45.110
All of it.

592
00:26:46.910 --> 00:26:49.130
But the hulking out, I can't picture.

593
00:26:49.790 --> 00:26:50.350
What?

594
00:26:50.530 --> 00:26:55.730
I mean, I'm always like, our purpose is to win, right?

595
00:26:55.830 --> 00:26:57.050
I'm here to win.

596
00:26:57.530 --> 00:26:58.090
Yes.

597
00:26:58.370 --> 00:27:00.430
So what's the problem?

598
00:27:04.400 --> 00:27:07.720
Yeah, I think they're looking for like a type of sportsmanship.

599
00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:08.940
What?

600
00:27:09.180 --> 00:27:16.360
Where when you're ahead so far, you know, you do maybe a little bit of what I...

601
00:27:16.360 --> 00:27:16.960
Take your foot off the gas.

602
00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:17.420
Yeah.

603
00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:20.220
You know, they call it like a gentleman's serve, right?

604
00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:21.120
Or like a...

605
00:27:21.120 --> 00:27:21.380
I know.

606
00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:23.520
Sometimes I really do try to do that.

607
00:27:23.680 --> 00:27:27.120
And then other times you just see the court and you see the shot and you take it.

608
00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:29.640
And you forget that you're up 7-2.

609
00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:31.140
You just see the shot.

610
00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:31.940
So you take it.

611
00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:33.200
I think it's fine.

612
00:27:33.380 --> 00:27:33.800
You know?

613
00:27:33.940 --> 00:27:34.820
I'm on your side.

614
00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:38.560
Listen, you have to know the two people that influenced my tennis career.

615
00:27:38.900 --> 00:27:42.260
One was Coach Lunn in high school.

616
00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:43.340
He coached basketball.

617
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:44.720
All he cared about was basketball.

618
00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:48.400
We went to state and we won state for men's basketball.

619
00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:51.320
So this was a big legacy of his.

620
00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:54.820
And then someone just told him, oh, and you also have to coach tennis.

621
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.560
And he was probably like, what the hell?

622
00:27:56.940 --> 00:27:58.000
Because he could give a shit.

623
00:27:58.220 --> 00:27:59.440
But he would drive me to matches.

624
00:27:59.720 --> 00:28:04.840
And right before I left the van to go to my game, as I got out of the van, he'd say,

625
00:28:04.940 --> 00:28:06.600
Kinsey, victory or death?

626
00:28:07.120 --> 00:28:07.800
That was it.

627
00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:09.020
Those are my only options.

628
00:28:09.280 --> 00:28:12.300
And then he would nap in the van, not even watch my match.

629
00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:15.280
And then after the match, I'd get in the van.

630
00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:16.520
He'd be like, victory or death?

631
00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:19.320
And if I said death, he'd say, stinking, Kinsey.

632
00:28:20.500 --> 00:28:21.400
Stinking, Kinsey.

633
00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:23.120
OK, so you have Coach Lunn.

634
00:28:23.260 --> 00:28:26.080
And then the biggest tennis influence in my life is my mom.

635
00:28:26.720 --> 00:28:30.360
My mother was an amazing, amazing tennis player.

636
00:28:30.540 --> 00:28:32.280
I'll never be as good as she was.

637
00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:35.100
And I just grew up watching her matches.

638
00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:39.860
And she has a very dear friend who she played tennis with, who is from the Netherlands, Karina.

639
00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:44.800
And her and Karina would say to each other before a doubles match, stick it in their ear.

640
00:28:44.800 --> 00:28:48.840
And so my mom will say to me before a match, go stick it in their ear.

641
00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:52.460
When I retell the story, I have to remember to really pronunciate ear.

642
00:28:52.740 --> 00:28:56.280
Because for a long time, my tennis friends thought I was saying, stick it in their rear.

643
00:28:56.660 --> 00:28:57.020
OK.

644
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.280
Stick it in their rear.

645
00:28:58.460 --> 00:28:59.200
So you hear it?

646
00:28:59.300 --> 00:28:59.800
I hear it.

647
00:28:59.900 --> 00:29:03.800
Anyway, so I have victory or death and stick it in their ear.

648
00:29:04.700 --> 00:29:06.120
This is where I come from.

649
00:29:06.280 --> 00:29:09.040
This is as you step onto the court.

650
00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:10.700
This is what's in my brain.

651
00:29:11.240 --> 00:29:15.300
Well, that makes sense for this next clip, maybe.

652
00:29:15.560 --> 00:29:17.940
Do you have it in your head even when you're warming up?

653
00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:20.040
I guess so.

654
00:29:20.160 --> 00:29:21.220
Even when you're warming up?

655
00:29:21.880 --> 00:29:22.400
Why?

656
00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:24.160
This is a leading question.

657
00:29:24.460 --> 00:29:24.940
I don't know.

658
00:29:25.120 --> 00:29:26.500
Do you remember the injury?

659
00:29:27.400 --> 00:29:28.380
Oh, no.

660
00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:29.380
Let's hear it.

661
00:29:29.420 --> 00:29:30.020
Oh, no.

662
00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:30.880
Oh, no.

663
00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:35.520
April, you're the only one here I think she's actually wounded?

664
00:29:36.060 --> 00:29:37.060
Yeah, I think so.

665
00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:37.880
I think so.

666
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.160
And I'm going to add during a warm-up.

667
00:29:40.800 --> 00:29:42.040
Like during a warm-up.

668
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:42.860
Not even.

669
00:29:43.200 --> 00:29:43.420
Yeah.

670
00:29:44.420 --> 00:29:49.560
No reason to come at me with like that fierceness.

671
00:29:49.740 --> 00:29:50.520
But yet she did.

672
00:29:50.880 --> 00:29:51.920
So yeah, I think.

673
00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:52.500
You had the net, right?

674
00:29:52.680 --> 00:29:54.880
And she hit really hard.

675
00:29:55.280 --> 00:29:57.060
Like right into my eye.

676
00:29:57.280 --> 00:29:57.620
Yeah.

677
00:29:57.900 --> 00:30:00.680
Like there was, I could not get my racket up in time.

678
00:30:01.780 --> 00:30:03.180
And she gave you a black eye.

679
00:30:03.560 --> 00:30:03.980
Yeah.

680
00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:04.480
Yeah.

681
00:30:04.740 --> 00:30:05.220
She did.

682
00:30:06.520 --> 00:30:07.860
She did do that.

683
00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:14.140
And then after that, like I think it was maybe your first time back after that or whatever.

684
00:30:14.500 --> 00:30:15.220
I was on her team.

685
00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.060
And April, obviously a little skittish.

686
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:19.780
And, you know, we were all like, okay, it's okay, April.

687
00:30:19.940 --> 00:30:27.560
And so you, you know, if you're not the Hulk, then you're like, I'm going to not hit it at April as much as I can.

688
00:30:27.560 --> 00:30:31.820
And if I do accidentally hit it towards you, I'd say, oh my gosh, I'm so sorry.

689
00:30:31.980 --> 00:30:33.540
You know, sort of an understanding.

690
00:30:34.060 --> 00:30:36.700
And the Hulk just kept coming back at you.

691
00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:38.000
Yes, she did.

692
00:30:38.220 --> 00:30:38.760
Yes, she did.

693
00:30:38.840 --> 00:30:40.500
It was more like an opportunity.

694
00:30:40.960 --> 00:30:42.220
To keep scoring.

695
00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:48.820
The thing that's amazing about her also is it's impossible to actually make her mad.

696
00:30:49.480 --> 00:30:50.680
Have you noticed that?

697
00:30:50.820 --> 00:30:51.600
And I try.

698
00:30:51.860 --> 00:30:52.980
That's a good point.

699
00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:53.700
Yeah.

700
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:55.120
That is a really good point.

701
00:30:55.340 --> 00:30:55.500
Yeah.

702
00:30:55.500 --> 00:31:00.800
If you come back at her with the shots that she hits at you, she just will tell you good shot.

703
00:31:01.480 --> 00:31:02.780
Oh, it's so irritating.

704
00:31:03.340 --> 00:31:03.720
It's really infuriating.

705
00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:07.840
Oh my gosh.

706
00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:08.800
I'm sorry.

707
00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:09.300
I'm laughing.

708
00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:13.120
So you busted this woman's face and then smelled blood in the water.

709
00:31:13.340 --> 00:31:13.820
Okay.

710
00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:15.320
And then pounced on the opportunity.

711
00:31:15.640 --> 00:31:22.240
First of all, one of the things they didn't mention, and ladies, how dare you, is that was a backhand.

712
00:31:22.240 --> 00:31:25.720
It was really, my backhand is not great.

713
00:31:25.900 --> 00:31:26.700
It's very inconsistent.

714
00:31:27.520 --> 00:31:31.260
So I'm always like, I can't believe that was a backhand.

715
00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:34.420
That's your takeaway from the story.

716
00:31:34.420 --> 00:31:35.080
Then not, I'm sorry.

717
00:31:35.220 --> 00:31:41.240
Is that, but the thing they didn't mention is how impressive that is for a backhand.

718
00:31:41.560 --> 00:31:42.320
For me.

719
00:31:42.580 --> 00:31:45.700
But no, I, of course, I felt horrible.

720
00:31:45.980 --> 00:31:48.940
And then a week went by and then April had a shiner.

721
00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:51.860
And I was like, oh my God, April, I'm so sorry.

722
00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:53.460
I just felt so bad.

723
00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:58.360
And then the next time we played, it was the same shot, a backhand.

724
00:31:58.500 --> 00:32:01.100
Like, and it, I almost hit her again.

725
00:32:01.320 --> 00:32:02.780
And I was like, oh my God, that's it.

726
00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:03.200
I can't.

727
00:32:03.280 --> 00:32:07.620
I'm like, I didn't, you don't mean to hit someone ever in tennis.

728
00:32:07.840 --> 00:32:08.300
Of course not.

729
00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:10.560
I mean, really, you don't.

730
00:32:10.880 --> 00:32:14.540
I mean, I think there's some people that go at people on purpose, but I don't.

731
00:32:14.620 --> 00:32:15.880
I wish I had the accuracy.

732
00:32:16.180 --> 00:32:16.560
I don't.

733
00:32:16.760 --> 00:32:19.100
I mean, I don't wish that I had the accuracy to hit someone.

734
00:32:19.420 --> 00:32:21.040
It's coming out a little.

735
00:32:21.040 --> 00:32:23.640
The Hulk is a little here.

736
00:32:23.740 --> 00:32:27.440
Also, do you know what is really annoying is that now they're going to call me the Hulk

737
00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:28.380
and I'm so pissed.

738
00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:31.200
I now have a new nickname.

739
00:32:32.280 --> 00:32:36.900
Well, lady, in addition to playing with your tennis ladies, you also started this year playing

740
00:32:36.900 --> 00:32:37.760
with USTA.

741
00:32:38.360 --> 00:32:38.760
Yes.

742
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:40.000
Do you want to tell people about it?

743
00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:40.520
Yeah.

744
00:32:40.620 --> 00:32:43.200
I mean, I think you guys out there probably know USTA.

745
00:32:43.460 --> 00:32:46.540
It's the United States Tennis Association and it's really fun.

746
00:32:46.540 --> 00:32:51.060
And I'm at the very beginning of this journey, but some ladies are really nice and some are

747
00:32:51.060 --> 00:32:51.740
total bitches.

748
00:32:53.480 --> 00:32:56.420
And we all kind of commiserate after the fact of like, wow.

749
00:32:57.620 --> 00:33:00.480
Well, I met a very nice lady who played you.

750
00:33:00.780 --> 00:33:07.980
I was in Tokyo and I was waiting for Lee and our daughter to get off of the 10th tallest

751
00:33:07.980 --> 00:33:08.760
roller coaster.

752
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:14.860
And a woman came up to me and she said, hi, are you Jenna Fisher from the office?

753
00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:15.860
And I said, yes.

754
00:33:15.860 --> 00:33:22.000
And she said, well, I just wanted to say that I played tennis with Angela Kinsey at USTA

755
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.520
and she's just the nicest person ever.

756
00:33:25.180 --> 00:33:29.320
So just so you know, you did leave a very good impression at USTA.

757
00:33:29.600 --> 00:33:31.000
I am nice, you guys.

758
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.040
I am nice.

759
00:33:32.120 --> 00:33:33.720
I'm just there to win.

760
00:33:34.120 --> 00:33:36.980
And again, April, I'm so sorry about your eye and I love you.

761
00:33:37.300 --> 00:33:41.880
Before we start the call sheet questions, there was one thing I was surprised the ladies didn't

762
00:33:41.880 --> 00:33:48.120
share, which is a lot of times when I do that little drop shot or the angle shot, they call

763
00:33:48.120 --> 00:33:48.600
me a cunt.

764
00:33:49.720 --> 00:33:53.980
But I think they were afraid to curse, but it's the highest form of praise.

765
00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:57.980
Like if any of us gets called that, we're like, thank you.

766
00:33:58.160 --> 00:33:58.880
Thank you very much.

767
00:33:59.060 --> 00:33:59.440
Uh-huh.

768
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:00.700
All right.

769
00:34:00.940 --> 00:34:01.080
Yeah.

770
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.940
In fact, we got Betsy a necklace.

771
00:34:04.340 --> 00:34:08.920
It looks like a gold charm, but if you get really close, it says cunt and she'll wear

772
00:34:08.920 --> 00:34:10.140
the necklace when we play.

773
00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:13.400
And when one of us does a shot, she's like, come kiss the necklace.

774
00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:19.120
Well, Angela, I think now it's time to move on to the call sheet questions.

